Z||000000||84Bill||04-18-2001||08:13 PM||||Where is the Cruise control module located and what does it look like?||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||04-18-2001||08:28 PM||||Bill, It looks like a silver/grey box and is located on the left side of the center hump next to the driver.  If you lift the carpet on the hunp on the left side you should see it.  Hope this helps.||||reg||12
Z||000002||84Bill||04-18-2001||10:11 PM||||Thanks!||||reg||10
Z||000003||Rodrv6||04-18-2001||10:34 PM||||Unless you have an 84. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Then it's integrated in the instrument cluster with the speedometer electronics.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||12
Z||000004||84Bill||04-19-2001||12:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodrv6:<BR><B>Unless you have an 84.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Then it's integrated in the instrument cluster with the speedometer electronics.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Are you sure about this? because I have an 84 SE and the car I'm pulling the cruise from is an 84 SE as well. does that mean that I can just plug in the stuff and go cruise?<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000005||Rodrv6||04-19-2001||05:57 AM||||About 9 years ago,I installed cruise in an 84 that didn't have it. As well as I can remember, I had to swap out the main wire harness, the engine room wire harness, and the instrument cluster.  The non-cruise car didn't have any of the cruise control wiring installed from the factory.  I think GM made a kit later on to install the separate cruise module like the newer Fiero's came with, but I don't know any details about it.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
